module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpChartCover.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ExceptionalCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierAffineLocalConverse.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Lift.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Lift.IdealComap

/-!
# The exceptional divisor on a named affine chart of the blowup

Let `X` be a scheme and `I` a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on it, with blowup `b : Bl_I(X) ⟶ X`.
On the standard chart `Spec Γ(X, U)[I/a] ⟶ Bl_I(X)` of [Stacks, Tag 0804], this file computes the
exceptional ideal sheaf `AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalIdeal I = I.comap b`: it is generated by the
single nonzerodivisor `chartGenerator`, the pullback of `a`.

That is the affine-local input of [Stacks, Tag 02OS (2)], whose scheme-level statement is
`Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal` — the declaration carrying the tag,
re-exported into this namespace below. The source's proof is *"By Lemma 0804 we see that `X'` is
covered by the spectra of the affine blowup algebras `A' = A[I/a]`. Then `IA' = aA'` and `a` maps
to a nonzerodivisor in `A'`"*, and the ring-level halves of that are
`Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra` and
`Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra`.

The only genuinely new step is identifying `Γ(Bl_I(X), W)` with `Γ(X, U)[I/a]` *compatibly with
the restriction map from `Γ(X, U)`*, where `W` is the chart's image: `appLE_chartOpen` below. That
is what lets `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` — which expresses the ideal of `I.comap b` on
an affine open `W` of the blowup as the image of `I.ideal U` under
`b.appLE U W : Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Bl_I(X), W)` — be read off the two ring-level chart facts.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartOpen`: the image of the chart, as an affine open of the blowup.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartΓIso`: the identification `Γ(Bl_I(X), W) ≅ Γ(X, U)[I/a]`.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartGenerator`: the generator of the exceptional ideal on the chart,
  as a *named* section — the pullback of `a` along the blowup morphism.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.exceptionalChartTrivialization`: the sectionwise trivialization of
  the exceptional ideal sheaf on the chart, "divide by `chartGenerator`".

## Main results

* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.appLE_chartOpen`: under `chartΓIso`, the restriction map
  `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Bl_I(X), W)` is the canonical map `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(X, U)[I/a]`.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.ideal_exceptionalIdeal_chartOpen`: on the chart at `a`, the exceptional
  divisor is cut out by `a`.
* `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of_isIso`: the reduction of
  [Stacks, Tag 0806] with **one** hypothesis left, namely [Stacks, Tag 02OS (1)].

## Implementation notes

**Why `appLE_chartOpen` is proved through `Spec` rather than by rewriting.** The natural route is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE` followed by rewriting the composite
`chart ≫ b` into `Spec.map (algebraMap …) ≫ U.fromSpec`. That rewrite is not available: the
inequality argument of `Scheme.Hom.appLE` has a type mentioning the morphism, so the motive is not
type-correct. Instead the identity is proved after applying `Spec`, where the morphism may be
rewritten freely, and then pulled back along `AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.map_injective`; the
cancellation of `U.fromSpec` is legitimate because it is an open immersion, hence a
monomorphism.

**An elaboration pitfall, in the §6 family.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.affineOpens` is a
`Set` of opens, so for `U : X.affineOpens` the projection `U.2` has type `↑U ∈ X.affineOpens`,
which is only *definitionally* `IsAffineOpen ↑U`. Dot notation `U.2.fromSpec` elaborates fine, but
instance search cannot unfold through the membership, so `IsOpenImmersion U.2.fromSpec` — and with
it `Mono U.2.fromSpec` — **fails to synthesize**, while the identical goal stated for a hypothesis
`hU : IsAffineOpen U.1` succeeds. The instance is supplied explicitly as
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isOpenImmersion_fromSpec U.2`. (`ResolutionOfSurfaces/FormalArcs`
works around the same thing with a `private` wrapper `isAffineOpen_coe`.)

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0806](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0806)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpUniversal

universe u

namespace Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U)

/-- The image of the standard chart at `a`, as an affine open of the blowup: it is the open range
of an open immersion whose source is affine. -/
def chartOpen : (blowUp I).affineOpens :=
  ⟨(chart I U a).opensRange, isAffineOpen_opensRange (chart I U a)⟩

/-- The chart's image lies over the affine open `U` of the base. -/
theorem chartOpen_le : (chartOpen I U a).1 ≤ blowUpToBase I ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx
  show blowUpToBase I (chart I U a z) ∈ U.1
  have h : (chart I U a ≫ blowUpToBase I) z =
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a))) ≫
        U.2.fromSpec) z := by rw [chart_blowUpToBase]
  rw [show blowUpToBase I (chart I U a z) = (chart I U a ≫ blowUpToBase I) z from rfl, h]
  exact U.2.range_fromSpec.le ⟨_, rfl⟩

/-- **The sections of the blowup on the standard chart at `a` are the affine blowup algebra
`Γ(X, U)[I/a]`.** The chart is an open immersion from `Spec Γ(X, U)[I/a]` whose image is
`chartOpen I U a`, so `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.ΓIsoTop` identifies the sections there
with the global sections of `Spec Γ(X, U)[I/a]`. -/
def chartΓIso : Γ(blowUp I, (chartOpen I U a).1) ≅ .of (chartRing I U a) :=
  (IsOpenImmersion.ΓIsoTop (chart I U a)).symm ≪≫ Scheme.ΓSpecIso _

/-- The identification of the previous definition is the restriction map of the chart, followed by
the canonical identification of the global sections of a spectrum. -/
theorem chartΓIso_hom_eq :
    (chartΓIso I U a).hom =
      (chart I U a).appLE (chartOpen I U a).1 ⊤
          (le_of_eq (Scheme.Hom.preimage_opensRange (chart I U a)).symm) ≫
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (chartRing I U a))).hom := by
  simp only [chartΓIso, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, IsOpenImmersion.ΓIsoTop, Iso.trans_inv,
    Functor.mapIso_inv, Iso.op_inv, eqToIso.inv, eqToHom_op, Iso.symm_inv,
    Scheme.Hom.appIso_hom', Scheme.Hom.map_appLE, chartOpen]

/-- The chart is recovered from `chartΓIso` as `Spec` of it, followed by the canonical morphism
from the spectrum of the sections on the chart's image. -/
theorem specMap_chartΓIso_hom_fromSpec :
    Spec.map (chartΓIso I U a).hom ≫ (chartOpen I U a).2.fromSpec = chart I U a := by
  rw [chartΓIso_hom_eq, Spec.map_comp, Category.assoc,
    IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec (chart I U a) (chartOpen I U a).2
      (isAffineOpen_top _), ← Category.assoc, IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top,
    ← Scheme.isoSpec_Spec_hom, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.id_comp]

/-- **The chart is `Spec Γ(X, U)[I/a]` over `X`, on sections.** The restriction map of the
structure sheaf from `U ⊆ X` to the standard chart at `a` is, under `chartΓIso`, the canonical map
`Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(X, U)[I/a]`.

This is the scheme-level statement `chart_blowUpToBase` read on sections. It is proved in that
direction — through `Spec` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.map_injective` — because the inequality
argument of `Scheme.Hom.appLE` mentions the morphism, so the morphism cannot be rewritten
underneath it. -/
theorem appLE_chartOpen :
    (blowUpToBase I).appLE U.1 (chartOpen I U a).1 (chartOpen_le I U a) ≫
      (chartΓIso I U a).hom =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a)) := by
  apply Spec.map_injective
  -- `U.2` has type `↑U ∈ X.affineOpens`, which is only *definitionally* `IsAffineOpen ↑U`, so
  -- instance search cannot see the open immersion through it; supply it as a local instance.
  have : IsOpenImmersion U.2.fromSpec := IsAffineOpen.isOpenImmersion_fromSpec U.2
  rw [← cancel_mono U.2.fromSpec, Spec.map_comp, Category.assoc,
    IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec (blowUpToBase I) U.2 (chartOpen I U a).2,
    ← Category.assoc, specMap_chartΓIso_hom_fromSpec, chart_blowUpToBase]

/-- `chartΓIso` carries the pullback of a section of `U` to its image in `Γ(X, U)[I/a]`. -/
private theorem chartΓIso_hom_appLE_apply (x : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    (chartΓIso I U a).hom
        ((blowUpToBase I).appLE U.1 (chartOpen I U a).1 (chartOpen_le I U a) x) =
      algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) x := by
  have := DFunLike.congr_fun (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (appLE_chartOpen I U a)) x
  rwa [CommRingCat.hom_comp] at this

/-- **On the standard chart at `a`, the section `a` restricts to a nonzerodivisor.** Under
`chartΓIso` it is the image of `a` in `Γ(X, U)[I/a]`, which is a nonzerodivisor by
`Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra` — the ring-level half of
[Stacks, Tag 02OS (2)]. -/
theorem appLE_mem_nonZeroDivisors :
    (blowUpToBase I).appLE U.1 (chartOpen I U a).1 (chartOpen_le I U a)
        (a : Γ(X, U.1)) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors Γ(blowUp I, (chartOpen I U a).1) := by
  have hreg := isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mp
    (Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1))
      (Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1))))
  rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right]
  intro y hy
  have h0 : (chartΓIso I U a).hom y *
      algebraMap Γ(X, U.1) (chartRing I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1)) = 0 := by
    rw [← chartΓIso_hom_appLE_apply, ← map_mul, hy, map_zero]
  have hzero : (chartΓIso I U a).hom y = 0 :=
    mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right.mp hreg _ h0
  have hid : ((chartΓIso I U a).hom ≫ (chartΓIso I U a).inv) y = y := by
    rw [(chartΓIso I U a).hom_inv_id]; rfl
  rw [CommRingCat.comp_apply] at hid
  rw [← hid, hzero, map_zero]

/-- **On the standard chart at `a`, the exceptional divisor is cut out by `a`.** This is
`I · Γ(X, U)[I/a] = a · Γ(X, U)[I/a]`
(`Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra`) transported
along `chartΓIso`, after `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE` has expressed the ideal of
`I.comap b` on the chart as the image of `I.ideal U`. -/
theorem ideal_exceptionalIdeal_chartOpen :
    (exceptionalIdeal I).ideal (chartOpen I U a) =
      Ideal.span {(blowUpToBase I).appLE U.1 (chartOpen I U a).1 (chartOpen_le I U a)
                   (a : Γ(X, U.1))} := by
  apply Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_injective (chartΓIso I U a)
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I (blowUpToBase I) U (chartOpen I U a)
      (chartOpen_le I U a), Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, appLE_chartOpen,
    Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, chartΓIso_hom_appLE_apply]
  exact Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U) (a : Γ(X, U.1))
    (Localization.Away (a : Γ(X, U.1))) a.2

/-- **The named generator of the exceptional ideal on the standard chart at `a`**: the pullback
of `a` along the blowup morphism, restricted to the chart's image. -/
def chartGenerator : Γ(blowUp I, (chartOpen I U a).1) :=
  (blowUpToBase I).appLE U.1 (chartOpen I U a).1 (chartOpen_le I U a) (a : Γ(X, U.1))

/-- The exceptional ideal on the standard chart at `a` is generated by `chartGenerator`. -/
theorem ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator :
    (exceptionalIdeal I).ideal (chartOpen I U a) = Ideal.span {chartGenerator I U a} :=
  ideal_exceptionalIdeal_chartOpen I U a

/-- `chartGenerator` is a nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem chartGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors :
    chartGenerator I U a ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(blowUp I, (chartOpen I U a).1) :=
  appLE_mem_nonZeroDivisors I U a

/-- **The exceptional ideal sheaf is sectionwise trivial on the standard chart at `a`**, with the
trivialization "divide by `chartGenerator`". This is the general-base counterpart of the
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocalConverse.trivialization` that the affine case of [Stacks, Tag 02OS (3)]
consumes in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/TwistOneIdealSheaf.lean`. -/
def exceptionalChartTrivialization :
    Stacks.SheafDescent.Trivialization (blowUp I).presheaf
      (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf
        (exceptionalIdeal I).subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom).val (chartOpen I U a).1 :=
  Stacks.CartierAffineLocalConverse.trivialization (exceptionalIdeal I) (chartOpen I U a)
    (chartGenerator I U a) (chartGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors I U a)
    (ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator I U a)

-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS (2)** is `Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal`,
-- which carries the tag; this is only this namespace's name for it, for the consumers that spell
-- it `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal`.
export Stacks.Blowup (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal)

/-- **The reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0806] with ONE hypothesis left.** The blowup of `X` in `I` is
a final object of the full subcategory of `Sch/X` whose objects have effective Cartier inverse
image of the centre, given only

* `hiso`: the blowup morphism is an isomorphism over the complement of the centre —
  [Stacks, Tag 02OS (1)].

The other hypothesis of `Stacks.Tag0806Lift.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of'''` — `hcartier`, which
is [Stacks, Tag 02OS (2)] — is `isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal` above.

**No `@[stacks 0806]` attribute is attached.** Tag 0806 carries a single unlabelled tag, so there
is no partial credit, and `hiso` is a hypothesis Tag 0806 does not grant: nothing in either tree
proves that `blowUpToBase I ∣_ supportCompl I` is an isomorphism. The source's proof of
[Stacks, Tag 02OS (1)] reduces it, via [Stacks, Tag 0805] (blowing up commutes with restriction to
an open subscheme), to the case `Z = ∅`, where the Rees algebra is
`⨁ₙ 𝒪_X` and the relative `Proj` is `X` itself — [Stacks, Constructions, Example 01MI]. -/
theorem nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of_isIso
    (hiso : IsIso (blowUpToBase I ∣_ supportCompl I)) :
    ∃ h : IsCartierOver I (Over.mk (blowUpToBase I)),
      Nonempty (IsTerminal (⟨Over.mk (blowUpToBase I), h⟩ : CartierOver I)) :=
  Stacks.Tag0806Lift.nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp_of''' I
    (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal I) hiso

end Stacks.BlowUpChartCover

end
